+# Aether IPW Metrics Patch
+
+This metrics-only patch adds a small Aether collection surface for
+GreenServe-style intelligence-per-watt experiments. It does not change
+SGLang scheduling, model execution, recompute/swap policy, or DVFS behavior.
+
+## Runtime Flags
+
+- `--enable-aether-metrics`: enable the JSON metrics endpoint.
+- `--aether-metrics-retain-events N`: keep the last `N` request metric events
+  in memory for experiment collection.
+
+## Endpoint
+
+When enabled, `GET /aether/metrics` returns:
+
+- `server`: model path, device, context length, tensor/data parallel size, KV
+  cache dtype, and max token pool settings.
+- `summary`: request count, prompt token total, completion token total, total
+  token total, aggregate E2E latency, average E2E latency, average TTFT, and
+  average TBT when SGLang exposes those fields.
+- `events`: recent request-level metric events with token counts, latency, and
+  finish reason.
+- `scheduler_info` and `internal_states`: existing SGLang scheduler/runtime
+  snapshots, included so Aether can correlate request metrics with KV capacity
+  and runtime state.
+
+## Patch Constraints
+
+- metrics are disabled by default
+- no scheduler behavior changes
+- no DVFS behavior changes
+- no extra dependencies in SGLang's default import path
+- CPU mode works in GitHub Actions for Aether integration tests
